id: pm-gh1365
title: "GH-1365: Agent UX: typed update refusals blame valid flags instead of the field that failed validation"
description: "Reported agent-facing contract defect imported from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1365. Preserve existing shipped foundations. Detailed source observations are dated 2026-09-30 and must be revalidated before implementation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: gh-1365,github-intake,sdk-first
created_at: "2026-10-02T17:09:15.472Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T12:45:03.514Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-03T12:45:02.903Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-03T12:45:02.903Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Risk, deadline and missing-ID fixtures identify the actual failure; Permuting valid title/priority flags never changes attribution; Attached values, aliases, multiple invalid inputs and no flagged inputs are covered; Error paths do not mutate item state; Unknown attribution is omitted; legal-domain values correspond to the blamed field; Existing policy-specific missing-field and surface tests remain green"
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "SDK validators own failed field, rejected value and enum-domain evidence; CLI guidance preserves producer attribution, canonical aliases, missing-ID operands and subcommand tokens without guessing from unrelated arguments. Get depth discloses its complete SDK domain. Compound projection conflicts identify their option surface while omitting an unknown scalar, and legacy inference only reads an argument already admitted by the matched invocation."
expected_result: "Risk and deadline refusals identify their own validator surface and rejected value; missing-item failures identify lookup or ID; valid unrelated title and priority flags never determine attribution, and unknown attribution is omitted."
actual_result: "Final corrected-source isolated suite: 9638 passed and two Windows-only cases skipped on Linux; exact coverage 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (66545/66545 statements, 50900/50900 branches, 13748/13748 functions, 63447/63447 lines). Full type checking, every static-quality stage including unchanged performance ceilings, graph/history and mutation controls (329 killed, seven reviewed equivalent, zero failures), native deduplicated linked tests, 58 clean packed Node/Bun manual commands with history verification, and nine npx/bunx packed package workflows plus typed SDK consumers passed. All 28 touched source functions have behavior-specific documentation. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passed with zero blocking issues, 1.40 percent finish error rate and zero missing error-code rows. Earlier failed test/coverage and performance observations remain recorded. Exact-head hosted checks/reviews and merge follow through PR1376; this batch is separate from the earlier v2026.10.3 publication and four pre-existing-main nightly alerts."
